      "writtenOn": "2023-08-15T18:07:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you explain why, CH? We\u0027d like to save power when the DRBG/SHA blocks are not being used. Is power management now handled internally by the ROM APIs? If not, shouldn\u0027t we turn the blocks on when calling trng_init and turn them off on trng_exit?",
      "parentUuid": "caf734d4_bf049fbb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 214,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "d721debc252d998a23b64aecf49f5d77dceed2b7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1ef1c7c_82f995ef",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/trng.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T03:25:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I understand correctly, with this CL\u0027s change, the DRBG/SHA is powered on in npcx_trng_hw_init and powered off in npcx_trng_power_off. \nDRBG-\u003egenerate should be always called after  npcx_trng_hw_init  and before npcx_trng_power_off. This why I think this is not required.\nIs my understanding correct?",
      "parentUuid": "4e88eeb4_7b42edfc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 214,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "d721debc252d998a23b64aecf49f5d77dceed2b7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7d1d3352_4a75a6a4",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/trng.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1551272
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T03:50:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"the DRBG/SHA is powered on in npcx_trng_hw_init\"\nYes\n\n\"DRBG-\u003egenerate should be always called after npcx_trng_hw_init and before npcx_trng_power_off\"\nAlso yes, but the current implementation in fpsensor.cc doesn\u0027t call npcx_trng_power_off. It does call trng_init and trng_exit something like this:\n\ntrng_init();\ntrng_rand();\ntrng_exit();\n\nThis is why I suggest trng_init() power on the blocks and trng_exit() power them off: to save power when not in use. This assumes the power API calls have small latency. Let us know your thoughts here.",
      "parentUuid": "a1ef1c7c_82f995ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 214,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "d721debc252d998a23b64aecf49f5d77dceed2b7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
